            B.q("ai-m5-28", "ai-pgvector", "Each learner has at most 2,000 notes, and every search is limited to one learner. What gives exact results with low compute?", listOf("An HNSW index on the embedding, with WHERE user_id = %s in the query", "An IVFFlat index with lists = 1, so every probe covers the learner's notes", "A GIN index on the embedding, combined with the user_id filter", "A B-tree index on user_id, then a distance sort over that learner's rows"), setOf(3), "When a filter narrows the search to a few thousand rows, an exact distance calculation over those rows is cheap and has perfect recall. A B-tree on the filter column finds the rows quickly; an approximate vector index is not needed.",
